{{Quote|The good news is we don't need a pickup because we found a new ''Phantom''.|Kanan Jarrus|<ref name="TLB" />}}
The '''''Phantom II''''' was a modified [[Sheathipede-class transport shuttle|''Sheathipede''-class transport shuttle]] belonging to the [[Spectres]]. It replaced the team's original [[VCX-series auxiliary starfighter]] ''[[Phantom]]'', which was lost during the [[Mission to Reklam Station|mission]] to [[Reklam Station]]. The Spectres acquired the ''Phantom II'' during a [[Mission to Agamar (2 BBY)|mission]] to the [[planet]] [[Agamar]], where they encountered a [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[Agamar garrison|holdout]]. Ambushed by the forces of the droid [[General]] [[Kalani]], the rebel away team was forced to engage in a live wargame with the droid army until both were attacked by an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] strike force. The Spectres kept the shuttle, modifying it for their own needs and repainting it. The shuttle was key to the success of several missions, including to [[Second mission to the third moon of Concord Dawn|Concord Dawn]] and [[Skirmish on Krownest|Krownest]].

By the [[New Republic]] era, the ''Phantom II'' was used to stop [[Transport CT-O5]] on [[Corellia]].

==Description==
{{Quote|We have three ''Sheathipede''-class shuttles, but they have no weapons.|General Kalani|<ref name="TLB" />}}
[[File:Phantom_II_pre_paint_job.png|thumb|left|200px|The ''Phantom II'', prior to its modification.]]
The ''Phantom II'' was a [[Sheathipede-class transport shuttle|''Sheathipede''-class shuttle]] in the Separatist military.<ref name="TP">{{TCW|Tipping Points}}</ref> The shuttle was also capable of traveling through [[hyperspace]]. After the [[Spectres]] rebel cell acquired the ship, they gave it a new paint job and upgraded it to include hull reinforcements, port and starboard forward cannons, ventral-mounted turrets, and an [[astromech socket]] located on the port side of the shuttle.<ref name="Imperial Super Commandos" /> The ''Phantom II'' was also modified to dock with the [[VCX-100 light freighter]] ''[[Ghost]]'' and served as the mother ship's [[shuttle]].<ref name="Iron Squadron">{{Rebels|Iron Squadron (episode)}}</ref> Despite its armaments and maneuverability, the ''Phantom II'' was still vulnerable to small-arms fire.<ref name="Legacy of Mandalore">{{Rebels|Legacy of Mandalore}}</ref>

==History==
===The Clone Wars===
The ''Phantom II'' was originally an unnamed and unarmed transport part of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems Navy|Confederate navy]], marshaled by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. The vessel was based on [[Agamar]]<ref name="TLB" /> after [[ST-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid|super tactical droid]] [[General]] [[Kalani]] was ordered to take his remaining [[Agamar garrison|forces]] to the [[planet]] by [[Count]] [[Dooku]].<ref name="TP" />

===Joining the rebellion===
[[Agamar garrison|Kalani's forces]] remained active in the [[Agamar system]] for [[Standard year|years]] until his forces were [[Mission to Agamar (2 BBY)|discovered]] by [[Spectres|members]] of the Rebellion. The [[droid]] [[C1-10P|Chopper]] found and restarted the [[shuttle]] while spying on several [[battle droid]]s. Chopper informed [[Ezra Bridger]] of the [[Starship|vessel]], and Bridger had the droid prepare the ship for departure. After realizing that the rebels and the droids were not each other's enemies, both parties joined together to successfully escape an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] assault. [[Kanan Jarrus]] realized the ship's potential<ref name="DB">{{Databank|phantom-ii|''Phantom II''}}</ref> and decided the commandeered vessel would serve as a replacement for the original ''[[Phantom]]'',<ref name="TLB" /> which was lost at [[Reklam Station]].<ref name="Steps">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Steps Into Shadow]]''</ref> The new ship was christened the ''Phantom II''.<ref name="TLB" />

[[File:PhantomII-SWX.png|thumb|left|250px|The ''Phantom II'' was updated with a new paint job and forward cannons.]]
After the [[Spectres]] returned to [[Phoenix Cell]] with the ship, the vessel underwent extensive modifications and upgrades. The shuttle was given a new paint job and upgraded to include hull reinforcements and an astromech socket located on the port side of the shuttle's now-shortened dorsal fin. The ship would be outfitted with port and starboard forward cannons, ventral-mounted turrets located adjacent to the boarding ramp,<ref name="Imperial Super Commandos" /> and would also modified to dock with the ''[[Ghost]]'' like the original ''Phantom''. This potentially allowed the ship to serve as the freighter's new rear gun but this was never observed in practice.<ref name="Iron Squadron" />

After communication with the [[Journeyman Protector|Protectors]] of [[Concord Dawn]] was lost, [[Sabine Wren]] led a [[Second mission to the third moon of Concord Dawn|recon mission]] with Ezra, [[Fenn Rau]], and Chopper to [[Concord Dawn]]'s [[Third moon of Concord Dawn|third]] [[moon]] to investigate the situation. Rau overpowered Sabine and Ezra and took the shuttle to a ridge overlooking the Protector camp, where he discovered his men had been killed by [[Imperial Super Commando]]s led by his rival, [[Governor]] [[Gar Saxon]]. While Sabine attempted to rescue Ezra from the traitorous Mandalorians, Rau stole the ''Phantom II'' and started to flee but returned and saved the Spectres after realizing Sabine was an honorable fighter who had risked her life to save others.<ref name="Imperial Super Commandos" />

[[File:Phantom2.png|thumb|right|250px|Fenn Rau pilots the ''Phantom II'' to rescue Sabine and Ezra from Gar Saxon.]]
The ''Phantom II'' later took part during the Phoenix rebels' [[Skirmish over Mykapo|evacuation]] of rebel sympathizers on [[Mykapo]]. [[Kanan Jarrus]] and [[Garazeb Orrelios]] used the ship to land on the planet to help with the evacuation before returning the ship to its port on the [[Ghost]]. After evacuating the rebel sympathizers, Jarrus’ lover [[Captain]] [[Hera Syndulla]], Bridger, Wren, and Chopper used the shuttle to travel to the [[Iron Squadron]] [[YT-2400 light freighter]] ''[[Sato's Hammer]]'' in an attempt to convince the Squadron to leave Mykapo before Imperial forces returned to the planet. Syndulla allowed Bridger, Wren, and Chopper to stay behind and repair the hyperdrive of the YT-2400 and convince the Iron Squadron to evacuate. When Imperial forces under [[Admiral]] [[Kassius Konstantine]] returned to the system, Ezra and Sabine managed to convince [[Gooti Terez]], [[Jonner Jin]], and [[R3-A3]] to escape on the ''Phantom II''. They were forced to leave Captain [[Mart Mattin]] behind after his ship was damaged by Imperial fire. After docking the ''Phantom'' with the ''Ghost'', the Spectres and Iron Squadron took part in a joint mission to rescue Mart.<ref name="Iron Squadron" />

Later, Jarrus and Wren used the ''Phantom II'' to follow Saxon’s old commanding officer, the renegade [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]], who flew his [[Kom'rk-class fighter/transport|Gauntlet fighter]] [[Nightbrother (Gauntlet fighter)|''Nightbrother'']] to his [[homeworld]] [[Dathomir]]. Maul coerced Bridger to come along. Prior to Maul's appearance at Chopper Base, Jarrus foresaw an issue with Bridger's behavior and had Wren install a [[Homing beacon|tracker]] on his [[wrist comm]], which was used to track him. The rebels landed the ship outside the [[Nightsister lair]] and ventured inside the cave to rescue Bridger, only to become possessed by the spirits of the [[Nightsisters]]. After defeating the spirits, Bridger and his friends resolved to stop Maul from [[Mission to Tatooine (Imperial Era)|reaching]] his archenemy [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], who held the [[Luke Skywalker|key]] to destroying the Sith.<ref name="Visions and Voices">{{Rebels|Visions and Voices}}</ref>

During the Spectres and the [[Captain]] [[Rex]]'s [[Mission to investigate Geonosis|second mission to Geonosis]], the ''Phantom II'' remained docked aboard the ''Ghost''. When [[Commander]] [[Saw Gerrera]] demanded that he take the [[Geonosian]] [[Klik-Klak]] on the shuttle for interrogation offworld, the Spectres and Rex opposed his demand.<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis">{{Rebels|Ghosts of Geonosis}}</ref>

The ''Phantom II'' would be docked aboard the ''Ghost'' as the ship departed Chopper Base for a training exercise. Following [[EXD-9]]'s [[EXD-9's infiltration of Chopper Base|attack]] on Chopper Base, the ''Phantom II'' and it's mother ship returned following Zeb's incident report.<ref name="Warhead">{{Rebels|Warhead (episode)}}</ref>

[[File:Zero_Hour_thumb.png|thumb|left|200px|The ''Phantom II'' attached to the ''Ghost'' during the [[Battle of Atollon]].]]
Later Sabine along with Kanan, Ezra, Chopper, and Fenn used the ''Phantom II'' to travel on a [[Skirmish on Krownest|mission]] to [[Krownest]], the home of [[Clan Wren]], to secure it's support for the Rebellion. The ship was attacked by Clan Wren warriors and sustained engine damage, but Sabine managed to land the ship in the snow. Chopper stayed aboard with Fenn while the others met with Countess [[Ursa Wren]] who was its leader and Sabine's mother. Chopper managed to repair the ship and used it to transport Kanan and Ezra back to the rebel forces after Sabine and Fenn stayed behind to help unify the Mandalorians.<ref name="Legacy of Mandalore" />

The ''Phantom II'' would be docked with the ''Ghost'' during the [[Battle of Atollon]],<ref name="Zero Hour">{{Rebels|Zero Hour}}</ref> a failed [[Mission to Jalindi|mission]] to [[Jalindi Station]] and the subsequent [[Mission to Faos Station|rescue of Ezra and Sabine]] from an incapacitated [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|Imperial Shuttle]] damaged by a massive [[kyber crystal]] explosion. The ship was still attached to the ''Ghost'' during its trip in hyperspace after the mission.<ref name="ITNOTR">{{Rebels|In the Name of the Rebellion}}</ref>

===Mission to Corellia===
[[File:Phantom_II-ToilAndTrouble.png|thumb|right|200px|The ''Phantom II'' chasing after Transport CT-O5]]
After the [[Attack on the Vesper]] which led to Nightsister survivor [[Lady]] [[Morgan Elsbeth]]'s liberation<ref name="M&A">{{Ahsoka|Part One: Master and Apprentice}}</ref>, Hera and Chopper traveled to the planet [[Corellia]] where they met with the rogue [[Regional Supervisor]] [[Myn Weaver]]. Upon learning ''[[Transport CT-O5|CT-O5]]'' was departing from the [[spaceport]], Hera boarded ''Phantom II'' and engaged the transport in a [[Starfighter combat|dogfight]]. Hera instructed Chopper to plant a [[homing beacon]] on the ship. When ''CT-O5'' was about to make the jump to hyperspace, Chopper swiftly planted a tracker on the ship.<ref name="T&T">{{Ahsoka|Part Two: Toil and Trouble}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The ''Phantom II'' first appeared in the ''[[Star Wars Rebels Season Three]]'' episode "[[The Last Battle]]," which debuted on [[Disney XD]] on [[October 22]], [[2016]].

